--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -41,3 +41,22 @@ The included `vercel.json` ensures:
 - **SPA Rewrites**: All paths rewrite to `/index.html` preventing 404 errors on deep page refreshes.
 - **Immutable Asset Caching**: High-performance HTTP caching for hashed Vite assets (`/assets/*`).
 - **Clean Bundling**: Hashed image assets (Edible Oil, Flour, Pasta shelves) bundled into `dist/assets/`.
+
+---
+
+## Bay Overlap De-duplication (multi-bay shelves)
+
+Reps shoot bays left to right, so the right edge of Bay N reappears at the left edge of Bay N+1. Each bottle is counted by exactly one bay:
+
+1. **Guide while shooting** – from Bay 2 on, the right 30% of the previous bay is shown faded on the left of the viewfinder. The viewfinder shows the full frame that will be saved (no hidden edges). Level-triggered auto-capture is off while the guide is shown.
+2. **Review before upload** – nothing is sent to n8n/Roboflow until the rep taps **Upload**. For Bay 2+, the app measures the overlap with the previous photo on the phone (`src/services/seamAlignment.ts`, ~150 ms, no extra Roboflow calls), shades it, and draws a **count line** in the middle of it. The rep can drag the overlap edge and tap **Check** to overlay the previous bay. Low-confidence measurements ask the rep to set the edge.
+3. **Counting** – Bay N keeps bottles whose box centre is left of its count line; Bay N+1 keeps bottles right of it. Bottles in the overlap are whole in both photos, so the cut never slices a bottle. Applied on POSM submit; on the Results bay tabs, red ✕ boxes are counted in the neighbouring bay (tap to count here too), green boxes are restored.
+4. **Records** – the Sheets discrepancy log gets an `[Overlap: Bay 1|Bay 2: 28% overlap (auto/high), 4 counted once]` note; `originalAiCounts` is the AI count after overlap removal, so only real rep edits appear as manual overrides. Each bay's `seam` is saved with the audit.
+
+### n8n (optional, recommended)
+
+Bay 2+ uploads include `bay_key`, `seam_cut_frac`, `seam_overlap_frac`, `seam_previous_bay`, `seam_confidence` and `seam_method`. The updated **Parse CV Output & Facing Counts** node in `n8n-mt-visit-audit-workflow.json` drops boxes left of `seam_cut_frac × image width` from `counts`, flags them (`excluded_by_seam`), and returns `counts_before_seam` + `seam_applied`. The app works with or without this node change.
+
+### Tuning
+
+Confidence thresholds and the guide width live at the top of `src/services/seamAlignment.ts` (`SCORE_*`, `MARGIN_*`, `GHOST_GUIDE_FRAC`). Tune them against real bay pairs with hand counts.
